text:
Arun Mehta: Heads-up from CloudPartner product: they want a compact 'marketplace-iac' reference that their marketplace team can import. Requirements: single TF module (marketplace_shim), tiny example app (Node.js), multi-arch guidance (arm64 + x86), optional KMS example, smoke CI, and a one-page onboarding. Keep the example HCL <200 LOC.
Celia Park: Sounds good. Let's make the repo easy to vendor: minimal code, Apache-2.0, and a clear CONTRIBUTING.md for SIs. Recommend module API: name, image, region, arch (arm|x86), enable_kms.
Tom Breuer: I'll draft the HCL. Plan: modules/marketplace_shim/{main.tf,variables.tf,outputs.tf}, examples/node/{index.js,package.json,Dockerfile}, ci/smoke.yml, docs/{README.md,ONBOARDING.md,COMPLIANCE.md}.
Yasmin Soto: Compliance note: include an explicit example of a KMS resource block and an audit sink placeholder. KMS must be opt-in (enable_kms = false by default). Document where secrets should come from.
Arun Mehta: CI should be GitHub Actions that runs terraform fmt -check, tflint, terraform init/plan, terraform apply (auto-approve) in a disposable workspace, then spin up the example container and curl /health. Keep smoke script bash-based (apply -> curl -> destroy).
Tom Breuer: Draft HCL for module (keeps it tiny):
```
# modules/marketplace_shim/main.tf
terraform {
  required_providers {
    partner = { source = "partnercloud/partner" version = ">= 1.0, < 2.0" }
  }
}
variable "arch" { type = string default = "x86" }
variable "enable_kms" { type = bool default = false }
locals { instance_map = { arm = "c7g.small" x86 = "c6i.small" } }
resource "partner_market_listing" "this" {
  name = var.name
  image = var.image
  instance_type = local.instance_map[var.arch]
  region = var.region
}
resource "partner_kms_key" "maybe" {
  count = var.enable_kms ? 1 : 0
  purpose = "ENCRYPTION"
}
output "listing_id" { value = partner_market_listing.this.id }
output "kms_key_id" { value = length(partner_kms_key.maybe) > 0 ? partner_kms_key.maybe[0].id : "" }
```
Yasmin Soto: Good. For COMPLIANCE.md include the KMS example and an audit log sink placeholder like `partner_log_sink.audit`. State that partners must configure their own log destination.
Celia Park: Example Node app should be intentionally tiny: /health and /invoke endpoints; invoke returns {"model_output": "stub"}. Dockerfile uses node:20-slim. Provide package.json with express only.
Arun Mehta: Add README matrix table for supported regions and recommended instance types per arch, and a short WARNING: "Do not use GPUs that require host-level driver installs; prefer cloud-managed GPU images."
Tom Breuer: Add .tflint.hcl and commit terraform.lock.hcl. CI will run tflint and terraform fmt -check to enforce style. Include sample vars.tfvars for CI so partner can copy/paste.
Yasmin Soto: ONBOARDING.md should be one page: fork -> pin providers -> run smoke CI -> create release tag -> submit PR to Redwood for verification. Also include how to run an arm smoke test (recommend cloud runners or qemu, warn about slowness).
Arun Mehta: Also include section on module semver and provider pinning with examples for required_providers and module source. Partners want to see how to pin before publishing.
partner-bot: Helpful checklist: https://redwood-internal/partner-checklists/marketplace-iac-reference (auto-post)
Celia Park: Ownership: Tom -> initial PR + HCL, Yasmin -> compliance docs, Arun -> runbook + release notes. We'll schedule a 30m pairing after PR if PartnerCloud wants a walkthrough.
Tom Breuer: I'll open the PR tonight and tag @Celia and @Yasmin. Keeping the examples minimal and dependency-free.
Arun Mehta: Thanks team. When PR is up post link here and we'll attach ONBOARDING.md to the partner ticket.
